cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MotoQuant Pro in research, please cite it as below."
title: "MotoQuant Pro: a first-principles motorcycle quarter-mile simulator"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mudhai
    given-names: Hritwik
    email: dhisetu@gmail.com
  - name: "The MotoQuant Pro contributors"
version: "4.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-15"
url: "https://motoquant.in"
repository-code: "https://github.com/da25mem5s02-debug/MotoQuant_v1"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - motorcycle
  - drag racing
  - vehicle dynamics
  - quarter mile
  - physics simulation
abstract: >-
  A Python physics engine (RK4 integration at 1 ms, Pacejka tyre model,
  clutch-slip launch dynamics, weight transfer, aerodynamic drag and
  density-altitude correction) that predicts motorcycle quarter-mile elapsed
  time and trap speed for a 541-bike catalog, validated against 250 published
  benchmarks. Data is licensed separately under ODbL 1.0; see LICENSE-DATA
  and docs/DATA_PROVENANCE.md for the caveats on estimated values.
